outputs.exact_statement:
For every $0<\eta<1/4$ there is $0<\beta_0<1/16$ with the following property. If $0<\beta\leq\beta_0$, then for every sufficiently large integer $m$ there are unit vectors $(a_x)_{x\in X}$ in $\mathbb R^m$, where $|X|=2m$, and signs $f(x)\in\{1,-1\}$ such that:*

1.  *the vectors with either sign form an orthonormal basis, and hence $$\label{eq:frame-cancellation}
     \sum_{x\in X} f(x)a_xa_x^*=0;$$*


2.  *if $S\subseteq X$ and $|S|\leq4\beta|X|$, the synthesis map $F_S:\ell^2(S)\to\mathbb C^m$, $F_Se_x=a_x$, satisfies $$\label{eq:sparse-gram}
     \left\lVert F_S^*F_S-I\right\rVert\leq\eta.$$*



*Moreover, for every sufficiently large integer $n$ there is a real orthogonal $n\times n$ matrix $O$ such that, on a set $Y$ of size $2n$, $$\label{eq:JZ}
 J=\begin{pmatrix}0&O\\ O^*&0\end{pmatrix},
 \qquad Z=\begin{pmatrix}I&0\\0&-I\end{pmatrix}$$ satisfy $$\label{eq:sparse-J}
 \left\lVert P_SJP_T\right\rVert\leq\eta
 \quad\text{whenever}\quad |S|,|T|\leq4\beta|Y|.$$ In particular, $J^*=J$, $J^2=Z^2=I$, $JZ=-ZJ$, and every diagonal entry of $J$ is zero.

There are numerical constants $C$ and $h_0>0$ such that, for the construction of Section <a href="#sec:construction" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="sec:construction">4</a> with $h\le h_0$ and $0<\eta\le1/4$, $$\label{eq:comparison}
 \left\lVert V_{qp}^{\{p,q\}}-V_{qp}^{\{p,q,r\}}\right\rVert
 \le Ch+CN\eta+CNh\eta$$ for every three configurations $p,q,r$. The constants do not depend on the cardinalities of any alphabets or on the configurations.

More precisely, for every nonamenable countable group and every $\delta>0$, we construct a separable Hilbert space $H$ and a normalized map $\mu:G\to\mathcal U(H)$ with $\operatorname{def}(\mu)<\delta$ such that $$\label{eq:distance-goal}
 \sup_{g\in G}\left\lVert\mu(g)-\rho(g)\right\rVert>\frac1{10}
 \quad\text{for every unitary representation }\rho:G\to\mathcal U(H).$$
